Dataiku API Logging & Infrastructure Configuration
**
### Meeting Objective
To configure, test, and validate end-to-end observability and query logging for Dataiku API endpoints across Staging and Production environments using Kubernetes and external S3 buckets.
### Key Discussions & Decisions
| Topic | Discussion & Resolution |
|---|---|
| **Infrastructure Configuration** | Modified the deployer node settings for Aura. Safely re-added the URL in the YAML configuration, enabled the duplicate log pod setting for troubleshooting, and set certificates to "Trust All Certificates". |
| **API Query Observability** | Configured endpoints to capture comprehensive query logs (success/fail statistics, request data, and responses). Unlike standard Dataiku resource logs, these API metrics are routed externally to an S3 bucket under the API monitoring path. |
| **Deployment & Pod Updates** | Logging changes applied at the infrastructure level do not automatically reflect on live endpoints. Endpoints must be explicitly updated (using the "Update" button, which triggers a rolling update with minimal downtime) so the Kubernetes pods recognize the new configuration. |
| **Production Environment Setup** | Confirmed the setup will be replicated in Production. The Event Server configuration will be centralized on the Production Design node, pointing to an isolated S3 connection/bucket path specific to Production to maintain data separation. |
| **Unified Monitoring Feature** | Jordan highlighted the Unified Monitoring panel found on the Deployer node's home screen (bird icon). This provides out-of-the-box monitoring for endpoint health, project status, and node alerting. |
### Testing & Validation
 * **Staging Validation:** Successfully redeployed a test API endpoint and sent test queries via Postman. Confirmed that the corresponding logs successfully appeared in the Dataiku dataset mapped to the S3 API monitoring path.
 * **Production Validation:** Set up a designated S3 dataset on the Production Designer node. Verified the connection and schema detection for future log parsing.
### Action Items
 * **Redeploy Remaining Endpoints:** Update all active API endpoints across the remaining infrastructures so they begin pushing query logs to the newly configured S3 datasets.
 * **Dashboard Configuration:** Import or build out the Advanced Analytics project within the Production environment to parse the incoming logs and expose them via monitoring dashboards.
 * **Resource Management:** Ensure any disabled or unused test API endpoints are properly updated to spin down their respective pods on the Kubernetes cluster.

